      "caption": "Grant Sabatier's wake up call came ten years ago, when he didn't have enough to buy a burrito for lunch. \u2060\n\u2060\nHe set a goal on the spot: earn $1 million and retire as early as possible. Doing anything he could to make money, like flipping domain names and Volkswagen campers, he boosted his income to more than $300,000 per year.\u2060\n\u2060\n\"I had 13 different income streams at one point,\" he tells @cnbcmakeit. What's perhaps even more impressive is he saved around 80 percent, letting it grow in the market.\u2060\n\u2060\nFive years, three months and six days later, he hit his target, and then some\u2060\u2014$1.2 million saved. His early retirement on that may not be comfy, but he has three tips for how to live sustainably in early retirement.\u2060\n\u2060\nRead more about his advice for early retirement at the link in bio.",
